1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,400
I want a partner like yours and I want friends like that guy and I want eyebrows like that girl.
她演绎一种比较的内心独白：“我想要像你那样的伴侣，像那个男生那样的朋友，还有像那个女生那样的眉毛。”

2
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:11,720
And I want his popularity and money I want her bravery and intelligence and happiness.
“我想要他的受欢迎程度和金钱，也想要她的勇气、聪明和幸福。”

3
00:00:12,399 --> 00:00:18,230
I don't actively think about comparing myself to these people but it's inevitable a natural instinct.
我不会刻意想着要和这些人比较，但她认为，这很难避免，是一种自然倾向。

4
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:24,150
As we collect information about our surroundings to evaluate how we're doing in life.
因为我们会收集周围的信息，评估自己生活得怎么样。

5
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:27,510
When I compare and I measure up I tend to feel good about myself.
当我比较后觉得自己比得上时，我往往会对自己感觉不错。

6
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:31,830
When I compare and I measure down I tend to feel bad about myself.
当我比较后觉得自己逊色时，我往往会对自己感觉不好。

7
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:41,280
Though not also comparison leads to envy envy always starts with self comparison but it goes far beyond simply wanting something.
这里字幕“though not also comparison”不清，似乎在说并非所有比较都带来嫉妒；她接着认为，嫉妒始于自我比较，但远超单纯想要某样东西。

8
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:47,120
See not only do I want what you have but I don't want you to have what you have.
她继续演绎：“你看，我不只想要你拥有的东西，我还不想让你继续拥有它。”

9
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:50,549
In fact I can't stand that you get to have it and I don't.
“事实上，我受不了你可以拥有它，而我却没有。”

10
00:00:50,559 --> 00:00:57,840
It's unfair I'm entitled to everything that everyone else gets to have why should I be any less.
“这不公平，别人能有的一切，我也有资格拥有，我凭什么就要差一点？”

11
00:00:57,840 --> 00:01:02,310
If you were a little bit less happy then I'll get to be happier.
“如果你没那么幸福，那我就能更快乐一点。”

12
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:07,670
And if your relationship wasn't going so damn well I would feel better about being single.
“如果你的感情没这么顺利，我对自己单身这件事就能好受些。”

13
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:10,560
Everyone seems to like you and speak so fondly of you.
“每个人似乎都喜欢你，提起你时也那么亲切。”

14
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:16,230
So when someone finally criticizes you it's deeply rewarding to me.
“所以，当终于有人批评你时，我会觉得特别解气。”

15
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:24,070
In fact you're not even that smart or pretty or funny or accomplished and you have something that I want.
“其实你根本没那么聪明、漂亮、有趣或有成就，却拥有我想要的东西。”

16
00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:34,080
I feel inferior to you so in order to at the very least feel equal to you I need to either bring you down or bring myself up.
“我觉得自己不如你，所以为了至少感觉与你平等，我就得把你拉下来，或者提升自己。”

17
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:42,550
And since it's easier bringing others down than it is working on lifting myself up that's what I will try to do.
“既然贬低别人比努力提升自己容易，我就会尝试那样做。”

18
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:49,429
Yeah so something like that is an example of how envy may play out in a person's mind.
对，类似这样，就是嫉妒可能在一个人脑海里上演的例子。

19
00:01:49,439 --> 00:01:52,550
Envy is when we see someone who has something that we want.
她把嫉妒解释为：我们看见别人拥有自己想要的某样东西。

20
00:01:52,560 --> 00:02:00,310
And so now we experience a gap between where we are and where we want to be what we have and what we want to have.
于是，我们感受到现实与期待之间的差距：现在在哪里、想去哪里，拥有什么、想拥有什么。

21
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:09,520
And it's how we respond to such gaps both emotionally and through our actions that we should pay very close attention to.
她认为，真正值得密切注意的，是我们在情绪与行动上如何回应这些差距。

22
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:17,269
So I like to think of envy as a spectrum where on one end it's very hostile so similar to what I just demonstrated.
所以，我喜欢把嫉妒看成一条连续光谱：一端很有敌意，就像我刚才演示的那样。

23
00:02:17,279 --> 00:02:20,400
And on the other end it's very non hostile.
而另一端，则非常没有敌意。

24
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:32,390
And I figured we could take a trip down memory lane to explore both ends with the help of some examples from my life.
我想，我们可以回顾一下往事，用我人生中的一些例子来探讨这两端。

25
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:45,040
So the prime of my envy was probably in my early teens and what I would envy the most was other girls looks and specifically their bodies.
我嫉妒心最强的时候，大概在十几岁出头；那时最羡慕的是其他女生的外貌，尤其是身材。

26
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:54,320
I was teased for being too skinny I don't think a day went by where someone did not make a comment about my weight and my body.
我曾因为太瘦而被取笑；我觉得几乎每天都有人评价我的体重和身体。

27
00:02:54,320 --> 00:03:03,199
Or at the very least someone would grab my wrist like this and say something like oh my god you're so skinny or watch out or you will break.
或者，至少也会有人这样抓着我的手腕，说“天啊，你好瘦”，或者“当心，你会断掉的”。

28
00:03:03,199 --> 00:03:07,510
Hi future lana here editing this video so they would actually grab it like this.
嗨，我是后来的 Lana，正在剪这支视频；他们实际上是这样抓的。

29
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:12,720
You know the good old circle grab that you use to determine how skinny someone is.
就是那种用手圈住手腕、判断一个人有多瘦的老动作。

30
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:16,720
So that you can then proceed to telling them that they are too skinny.
然后就接着告诉对方，他们太瘦了。

31
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:26,710
And I remember liking this boy when I was like 15 and him not wanting to be with me because he said that I did not look womanly enough.
我还记得，大约十五岁时喜欢过一个男生，但他不想和我在一起，因为他说我看起来不够有女人味。

32
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:36,240
And then he sent me a photo of another girl's body to show me what a real woman is supposed to look like.
然后他发来另一位女生身体的照片，想向我展示所谓“真正的女人应该长什么样”。

33
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:42,080
And I remember saving that photo and looking at it over and over again.
我记得自己保存了那张照片，一遍又一遍地看。

34
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:51,530
Wishing that I looked like that and I would resent the girl in that photo or really any girl whose body looked like hers.
希望自己也长得那样，并怨恨照片里的女生，或者说，任何身材和她相似的女生。
